OL,3,GNEWSAWoman hit by e-bike calls for more
OL,4,Apolice action
OL,5,
OL,6,FSussex Police has launched a new
OL,7,Foperation to tackle the illegal use of
OL,8,Fe-bikes and e-scooters in response to
OL,9,Fcommunity concerns and an increase in
OL,10,Freported incidents.
OL,12,FIn the 12 months up to June, the force
OL,13,Freceived a total of 2,504 reports of
OL,14,Fthe vehicles being ridden illegally -
OL,15,Fan increase of 53.7% from the 1,629
OL,16,Freports received during the previous
OL,17,Fyear.
OL,19,FE-bikes must meet certain requirements
OL,20,Fto be legal, while e-scooters cannot be
OL,21,Fused on public roads unless through an
OL,22,Fauthorised rental scheme.
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
